{173}{Yes...for as many generations as have been recorded in our family tome, the Schuylers have walked with the spirits of the dead.  My great-great-great grandfather was Conjurer-Witness to the chiefs of the Clan Wars, where the great machines of the dwarves leveled cities and mountains...}{Yes...for as many generations as have been recorded in our family tome, the Schuylers have walked with the spirits of the dead.  My great-great-great grandfather was Conjurer-Witness to the chiefs of the Clan Wars, where the great machines of the dwarves leveled cities and mountains...}{}{}{}{}
{174}{Interesting...please continue...}{}{5}{}{177}{}
{175}{I see.  Let's talk about these zombies.  They're your work?}{}{5}{}{83}{}
{177}{I told you before, we can trace our history back to the Age of Legends, where the great Necromancers ruled along with the Elven Council.  The days when mighty Kerghan, perhaps the first of our kind, battled the Bane of Kree in the Dead Hollows, and the very stones burned there for three days in their passing...}{I told you before, we can trace our history back to the Age of Legends, where the great Necromancers ruled along with the Elven Council.  The days when mighty Kerghan, perhaps the first of our kind, battled the Bane of Kree in the Dead Hollows, and the very stones burned there for three days in their passing...}{}{}{}{}
{178}{That's fascinating.  How did you go into business?}{}{5}{}{181}{}
{179}{And these zombies?  You're responsible?}{}{5}{}{83}{}
{181}{Oh, it's just the way things happen.  My grandfather, Basil Schuyler, decided he was tired of the stigma which had risen around our family.  You know, most people tend to stay away from Necromancers as a general rule...}{Oh, it's just the way things happen.  My grandfather, Basil Schuyler, decided he was tired of the stigma which had risen around our family.  You know, most people tend to stay away from Necromancers as a general rule...}{}{}{}{}
{182}{Yes, I can see why.  And so...?}{}{5}{}{184}{}
{184}{Well, he moved to Caladon and started a small business there.  P. Schuyler and Sons.  My father and my uncle were both still fairly young, but powerful in the arts.  They used their powers to locate lost artifacts, and made a business of selling unique and rare jewelry.  As you can see, the business has done fairly well.}{Well, he moved to Caladon and started a small business there.  P. Schuyler and Sons.  My father and my uncle were both still fairly young, but powerful in the arts.  They used their powers to locate lost artifacts, and made a business of selling unique and rare jewelry.  As you can see, the business has done fairly well.}{}{}{}{ru 2035}
{185}{I should say so.  Your family built this store over the tomb?}{}{5}{}{90}{}
{186}{And what about this business with the Eyeless Five?}{}{5}{gf1025 1, lf9 0}{189}{lf9 1}
{187}{I've heard rumors about a gem dealer from Arland...}{}{5}{gf1025 1, lf10 0}{193}{lf10 1}
{189}{The Eyeless Five were a strange case...one that was never solved by the authorities, and was only associated with us because of the sale of the ruby pendants.  We had nothing to do with the murders whatsoever.  It may have been done merely to bring us unwanted attention...sometimes businessmen are worse than the most hardened criminals...}{The Eyeless Five were a strange case...one that was never solved by the authorities, and was only associated with us because of the sale of the ruby pendants.  We had nothing to do with the murders whatsoever.  It may have been done merely to bring us unwanted attention...sometimes businessmen are worse than the most hardened criminals...}{}{}{}{}
{190}{I see.  And the gem dealer from Arland?}{}{5}{lf10 0}{193}{lf10 1}
{191}{Strange, I must say.  Your family built this store over the tomb?}{}{5}{}{90}{}
{193}{That man was sick before we ever saw him.  Our meeting was a legitimate business transaction.  His death following it was, unfortunately, an inevitability brought about by his weak constitution.}{That man was sick before we ever saw him.  Our meeting was a legitimate business transaction.  His death following it was, unfortunately, an inevitability brought about by his weak constitution.}{}{}{}{}
{194}{And the Eyeless Five?}{}{5}{lf9 0}{189}{lf9 1}
{195}{I see.  So, your family built this store over the dwarven tomb?}{}{5}{}{90}{}
{200}{Really?  Any more monstrous than the loggers who tear up trees inhabited by the spirits of elven holy men?  Or the great industrialists who blast train tunnels through the sacred blood stones of the old Ogre tribes?  Our small enterprise here can barely be called monstrous...}{Really?  Any more monstrous than the loggers who tear up trees inhabited by the spirits of elven holy men?  Or the great industrialists who blast train tunnels through the sacred blood stones of the old Ogre tribes?  Our small enterprise here can barely be called monstrous...}{}{}{}{}
{201}{True.  True.  Still, your business here is a bit on the odd side.}{}{5}{}{94}{}
{202}{Your justifications are flimsy. I'd guess your mettle is the same.}{}{5}{lc2 0}{223}{}
{203}{Your justifications are flimsy. I'd guess your mettle is the same.}{}{5}{lc2 1}{}{co, fl 238}
{208}{This tomb is from a clan long forgotten...the very fact that it lies here in the lowlands, and not the mountains, says that they were more than likely considered a lesser dwarven people.  In fact, it's a strong possibility they were outcasts...you know a dwarves true home is ALWAYS in the hand-carved caverns of mountain stone...}{This tomb is from a clan long forgotten...the very fact that it lies here in the lowlands, and not the mountains, says that they were more than likely considered a lesser dwarven people.  In fact, it's a strong possibility they were outcasts...you know a dwarves true home is ALWAYS in the hand-carved caverns of mountain stone...}{}{}{}{}
{209}{Well, I'm convinced.  Maybe we can come to an agreement?}{}{5}{}{110}{}
{210}{I don't buy it.  How can you be sure?}{}{5}{pa -6411}{213}{}
{211}{My friend Magnus, here, might take offense to your words.}{}{5}{pa 6411}{213}{}
{213}{I'm sorry, but look at the evidence.  The quality of the stonework here is shoddy, most of the jewelry we bring up out of here is so poorly made that we have to melt it down for our own uses, and look!...there's no writing on the walls...these dwarves may very well have been illiterate...}{I'm sorry, but look at the evidence.  The quality of the stonework here is shoddy, most of the jewelry we bring up out of here is so poorly made that we have to melt it down for our own uses, and look!...there's no writing on the walls...these dwarves may very well have been illiterate...}{}{}{}{}
{214}{That's a strong argument.  Can we come to an understanding?}{}{5}{}{110}{}
{215}{Wait!  You're talking about an old, proud people here!}{}{5}{pa -6411}{218}{}
{216}{Hold on!  These were Magnus' forefathers! }{}{5}{pa 6411}{218}{}
{218}{I'm sorry, but the proof is irrefutable!  Look at these dwarven zombies....all of their foreheads are sloped, many have physical defects like extra toes, the eyes are very close together.  No dwarf would possibly claim these freakish dwarves as their people!}{I'm sorry, but the proof is irrefutable!  Look at these dwarven zombies....all of their foreheads are sloped, many have physical defects like extra toes, the eyes are very close together.  No dwarf would possibly claim these freakish dwarves as their people!}{}{}{}{}
{219}{You've sold me.  Can we reach an understanding?}{}{5}{}{110}{}
